TITLE:: REScoreEditor
summary:: The transport and the editing of a folder of takes for a page (the lanes view)
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REScore, Classes/REScoreRecorder, Classes/REScorePlayer, Classes/REScoreVisuals

DESCRIPTION::
The live side of a page that shows, plays and edits the takes of a folder: HomewareSC's lanes view (code::scripts/rig/page/view.html::, served by the remote rig on a try's scores, and by code::scripts/take.sh view <folder>:: on a piece's Scores folder). It installs plain OSCdefs under code::<prefix>/rec/:: (never recorded), answers them on the song, keeps the take being edited as a working copy next to it (code::<take>.edit.json::, what the page shows and Play plays), and feeds the page's server back (code::/rigfeed/state:: four times a second, code::/rigfeed/edit:: after each operation, code::/rigfeed/event:: after each recorded event) unless a feed function is given. The protocol is the header of the class file:

list::
## code::<prefix>/rec/play <take|last>::, code::<prefix>/rec/stopPlay::: the take replays on the song (as edited while it is being edited); link::#-onPlayer:: receives the player.
## code::<prefix>/rec/edit <take> <op json>::: an operation (link::Classes/REScore#-edited::) applied to the copy.
## code::<prefix>/rec/undo <take>::: the last operation taken back (the file's score with the others applied again).
## code::<prefix>/rec/save <take> [new]::: the copy written over the take, or as a new file (code::<stamp>_<song> <version> edit.json::); the copy dropped.
## code::<prefix>/rec/revert <take>::: the copy dropped.
::
A take is named by its file name under the root or by its path; "last" is the recorder's last take.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: song
The link::Classes/RCSong:: the takes play on.
argument:: recorder
The song's link::Classes/REScoreRecorder:: (its last take is "last", its version names a new file, its events reach the feed; nil: none).
argument:: root
The folder of the takes (the recorder's when nil).
argument:: prefix
The OSC paths' prefix, code::/<song name>:: by default (the remote rig uses code::/rig::).
argument:: version
The version in a new file's name (the recorder's, "w0").
argument:: feed
A function code::{ |kind, dict| }:: called instead of sending the feed (the rig's own feed); nil: the feed is sent to feedPort, with the state and the recorder's events.
argument:: feedPort
The page server's feed port (32347).

METHOD:: workingPath
code::<take>.edit.json:: for a take's path.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: play
argument:: which
A take's name, path or "last".
argument:: quant
Returns the link::Classes/REScorePlayer::: an link::Classes/RERenderedPlayer:: when the take has a render next to it (code::<take>.render.json::, link::Classes/REScore#*readRender::) whose WAV exists and link::#-playRendered:: allows it; a take being edited is played by the program (its render is stale).
METHOD:: playRendered
code::\auto:: (the default: the render when its WAV exists), code::true:: (always), code::false:: (never: the program plays the take).
METHOD:: isPlayingRender
True while the player plays a render.
METHOD:: stopPlay
METHOD:: edit
argument:: which
argument:: op
A dictionary (link::Classes/REScore#-edited::).
METHOD:: undo
METHOD:: save
argument:: which
argument:: asNew
Returns the path written.
METHOD:: revert
METHOD:: takes
The takes under the root (companions, working copies and the files of a render left out: link::Classes/REScore#*isCompanion::), sorted.
METHOD:: resolveTake
A take's path from its name, path or "last"; nil (with a warning) when there is none.
METHOD:: state
What the page's state needs: recorder, beat, events, recBeat, position, playing, rendered, overdubbing, takes, lastTake, editing.
METHOD:: feed
A message of the feed (the function, else code::/rigfeed/<kind> <json>::).
METHOD:: onPlayer
code::{ |player| }:: when a replay starts (the remote rig attaches its visuals and its sliders' feed there).
METHOD:: player
METHOD:: playingPath
METHOD:: editing
The take being edited: code::(path:, original:, score:, ops:):: or nil.
METHOD:: free
The OSCdefs freed, the feed stopped and the recorder's onEvent put back, the replay stopped, the working copy dropped.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// a piece: its recorder made, the page served by scripts/take.sh view "<piece>/Scores"
~ed = REScoreEditor(~song, ~rec);          // prefix /<song name>, the recorder's folder
// the page's Play, Stop, edit, Undo, Save, Save in new file and Revert work from here on
~ed.play("last");                          // or from the IDE
~ed.edit("last", (op: "moved", id: 12, beat: 8.5));
~ed.save("last", asNew: true);
~ed.free;
::
